Though men have been wearing their suits with running shoes and incorporating sweatshirts into work gear for a while now, the athletic look continues this spring. Miuccia Prada presented a collection of what seemed to be team uniforms for the future. Valentino, Bottega Veneta and Raf Simons showed the majority (if not all) of their looks with sneakers instead of proper oxfords. Some designers were even more specific with their sporty adaptions — as in the case of the young British designer Lou Dalton, who created this high-fashion take on a baseball shirt ($399;
openingceremony.us
).
To be clear, these are not clothes meant for wearing on the field or court. Instead, worn a piece or two at a time, in muted tones (leave the neons at the gym), and paired with crisp shirts and neat trousers, they can add graphic interest to the most basic wardrobe. Raf Simons shirt, $430, and pants, $515;
rafsimons.com
.
